preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = average(h - l, rangeLookback), written lowercase as the
// feature register does (EasyLanguage is case-insensitive).
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808)
// and h - l is a PRICE expression with real history, so this is a fresh
// loop over price -- not the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator and not a
// mirrored variable buffer. Window INCLUSIVE of the current bar. Summed
// newest-first, EL's Summation order, exactly as NarrowRangeBar does.
//
// The threshold is in PRICE units: the book's "under a dollar of daily range"
// is a stock, where a point is a dollar. There is deliberately no
// BigPointValue factor -- that, plus range instead of TRUE range and a fresh
// mean instead of the rolling accumulator, is what separates this from
// AtrDollarsBelow.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[i] - low[i];
}
avgRange /= (int)rangeLookback;
